+
+# LOSSY-VERIFICATION PILOT PATCH (not upstream vLLM). "Reflective
+# verification via extended verification span" (RV) -- see
+# gpu_model_runner.py's own RV module comment for the full motivation and
+# the round layout. That comment for the other half explains WHY (every
+# threshold-gated variant of free-judgment tried this session -- trend-
+# based pivot, per-round reject-and-resample -- hurt more real cases than
+# it helped; RV drops the judge/threshold entirely and blends a fixed
+# "keep going" nudge into the target distribution unconditionally, every
+# round, modeled on Reflective Verification, arXiv:2505.18629). This half
+# reads target_logits at the duplicate-draft span (z_reflect), blends it
+# with the real span's own logits (z0) at the LOGIT level -- NOT
+# probability level, softmax is nonlinear so mixing probabilities and
+# mixing logits-then-softmax are genuinely different operations, and the
+# paper's own construction is explicitly the latter -- and REPLACES
+# target_probs at the real positions with the blended result BEFORE
+# spec-casc-tok's own eta/pi_rej math runs, so both the accept test (the
+# kernel reads target_probs directly) and the recovery/residual draw
+# (sample_recovered_tokens, fed recovery_target_probs which is built FROM
+# target_probs) use the nudged distribution -- closing the exact gap
+# reject-and-resample had: a rejected token there gets resampled from a
+# distribution that's already been nudged toward "keep going", not
+# resampled from the same untouched state that produced the bad draft.
+#
+# Unconditional by design: unlike every acted-on variant of free-judgment,
+# there is no judge, no score, no threshold, no trigger to get wrong. The
+# blend runs every round the layout is structurally present, at a fixed
+# alpha. This is a deliberate response to this session's own repeated
+# finding that no per-round transform of a judgment signal separates
+# "needs it" from "doesn't" -- RV sidesteps that problem instead of
+# solving it, by never having to decide WHEN to intervene.
+_RV_REAL_DRAFT_LEN_FILE = f"/tmp/lossy-token-eff-rv-real-draft-len-{os.getuid()}"
+try:
+    with open(_RV_REAL_DRAFT_LEN_FILE) as _f:
